#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid "Layouts: standard, compact, wide, two_columns, cards, minimal. header=\"no\" hides supported headings. Without lang, WordPress/the language plugin selects the language. The admin guide lists parameters/defaults. Editors preserve other translations. Guest payments are not linked to accounts by email."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid "Donation/support forms accept campaign_id=\"1\" to allocate payments to an open, unexpired campaign. Amounts are EUR 0.50-999,999.99 with up to two decimal places. Confirmed partial refunds reduce received totals; fully refunded, failed and pending payments are excluded. Expenses are entered separately by staff with manage_options."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid "WP-Cron prepares new PayPal plans in the background; retry shortly if requested. Empty secret fields retain saved values; replace them when changing account/environment."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid "Only verified payment events count as income; approval and return URLs do not. Cancellation stops future billing after the provider acknowledges it and does not refund previous payments. Closing a campaign prevents new payments/agreements but does not cancel existing agreements."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid ""
"Additional recurring events:\n"
"Stripe: invoice.payment_succeeded, invoice.payment_failed, customer.subscription.created, customer.subscription.updated, customer.subscription.deleted.\n"
"PayPal: PAYMENT.SALE.COMPLETED, PAYMENT.SALE.REFUNDED, BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.CREATED, BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.ACTIVATED, BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.CANCELLED, BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.EXPIRED, BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.SUSPENDED, BILLING.SUBSCRIPTION.PAYMENT.FAILED."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid ""
"One-time events:\n"
"Stripe: checkout.session.completed, charge.refunded.\n"
"PayPal: PAYMENT.CAPTURE.COMPLETED, PAYMENT.CAPTURE.REFUNDED."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid ""
"PayPal REST apps: https://developer.paypal.com/dashboard/applications/\n"
"Use a matching Client ID, Secret, Webhook ID and Sandbox/Live environment. For testing, use a Sandbox Business seller and a separate Personal buyer. PayPal Webhooks Simulator events are not a substitute for a real Sandbox checkout."
msgstr ""

#. Found in installation paragraph.
msgid ""
"Stripe API keys: https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys\n"
"Stripe webhook endpoints: https://dashboard.stripe.com/webhooks\n"
"Use snapshot events for your account, with matching test/live credentials. Thin events are not supported."
msgstr ""

